  "title": "Flexible, Scalable, High Channel Count Stereo-Electrode for Recording in the Human Brain",
  "description": "Intracranial EEG (iEEG) recordings used to evaluate a flexible, scalable, high-channel-count micro-stereo-electrode for recording neural activity in the brain. The dataset includes raw and preprocessed (epoched) recordings from multiple species, including human patients, non-human primates, pigs and rodents. Direct electrical stimulation was used to examine the effects of stimulation on brain activity. Data are organized in iEEG-BIDS format, with binary files and channel maps in the derivatives folder.",
  "methods_description": "Intracranial recordings were acquired with novel high-resolution micro-stereo-electrodes in human patients, non-human primates, pigs and rodents. Direct electrical stimulation tests were performed, and the data were epoched for preprocessing.",
